{"abstract":"Testing underwater vehicles in operational conditions is expensive. Formal models can lower the cost of operational testing and validation for these systems, as they allow detecting problems earlier. We propose modeling the underwater vehicle’s behavior as Timed Automata, and discuss examples of property patterns which can be handled by observer Timed Automata and Timed CTL properties. The goal is to build a set of specifications which can then be used for testing and validation of controllers in underwater vehicles.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Quijano, Sergio","Varshosaz, Mahsa","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818239"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Control","Model based testing","Safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and safety analysis of autonomous underwater vehicles behaviors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85205990497","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No 956200 REMARO, Reliable AI for Marine Robotics."],"id":"S01-000.00-818239","identifier":[{"id":"85205990497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-54cb5410-342b-4b42-b37c-8c48b63e83aa"],"keyword":["Model-based testing","Safety","autonomous underwater robots","control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-782E16DA0A2E62010F50CB0315AA07C8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergio","key":"quijanopau","last":"Quijano","locid":"fc57a764-276e-463a-aa68-fa54ffaf31d6","name":"Quijano, Sergio","orcid":"0000-0002-2138-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icstw60967.2024.00022","eisbn":["9798350344790"],"status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE International Conference on Software Testing, Verification and Validation Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205990497"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-54cb5410-342b-4b42-b37c-8c48b63e83aa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modeling and Safety Analysis of Autonomous Underwater Vehicles Behaviors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818239","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Varshosaz, Mahsa","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718913"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards formal specification of reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718913","ids":["itu-c1a10abd-9db2-4146-815d-57736cc40085"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E5D2FB9830E288FC9C228A74AAE03914"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1a10abd-9db2-4146-815d-57736cc40085"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Formal Specification of Reinforcement Learning","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718913","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The development process for reinforcement learning applications is still exploratory rather than systematic. This exploratory nature reduces reuse of specifications between applications and increases the chances of introducing programming errors. This paper takes a step towards systematizing the development of reinforcement learning applications. We introduce a formal specification of reinforcement learning problems and algorithms, with a particular focus on temporal difference methods and their definitions in backup diagrams. We further develop a test harness for a large class of reinforcement learning applications based on temporal difference learning, including SARSA and Q-learning. The entire development is rooted in functional programming methods; starting with pure specifications and denotational semantics, ending with property-based testing and using compositional interpreters for a domain-specific term language as a test oracle for concrete implementations. We demonstrate the usefulness of this testing method on a number of examples, and evaluate with mutation testing. We show that our test suite is effective in killing mutants (90% mutants killed for 75% of subject agents). More importantly, almost half of all mutants are killed by generic write-once-use-everywhere tests that apply to any reinforcement learning problem modeled using our library, without any additional effort from the programmer.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Varshosaz, Mahsa","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718929"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formal specification and testing for reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718929","identifier":[{"id":"85170641997","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57A3A50D8022ABBDAEC486C17E7459DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102788488/23-icfp.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3607835","issn":["24751421"],"issue":"Issue ICFP","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"125-158","paperid":"193","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"7"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170641997"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formal Specification and Testing for Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718929","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Linux Kernel is a world-class operating system controlling most of our computing infrastructure: mobile devices, Internet routers and services, and most of the supercomputers. Linux is also an example of low-level software with no comprehensive regression test suite (for good reasons). The kernel's tremendous societal importance imposes strict stability and correctness requirements. These properties make Linux a challenging and relevant target for static automated program repair (APR). Over the last decade, a significant progress has been made in dynamic APR. However, dynamic APR techniques do not translate naturally to systems without tests. We present a static APR technique addressing sequential locking API misuse bugs in the Linux Kernel. We attack the key challenge of static APR, namely the lack of detailed program specification, by combining static analysis with machine learning to complement the information presented by the static analyzer. In experiments on historical real-world bugs in the kernel, we were able to automatically re-produce or propose equivalent patches in 85% of the human made patches, and automatically rank them among the top three candidates for 64% of the cases and among the top five for 74%.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz, Alfredo","Varshosaz, Mahsa","Le Goues, Claire","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382107"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University"],"keyword":["Automatic Program Repair","Bugs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patching locking bugs statically with crayons","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382107","identifier":[{"id":"85162003734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-390a76e2-8df8-4f47-a492-3f53d89714bd"],"keyword":["Automatic Program Repair","Bugs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E793693139BFD8F2F8392EB6E39C492"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336666/3548684.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"cruzpau","last":"Cruz","name":"Cruz, Alfredo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"legouespau","last":"Le Goues","name":"Le Goues, Claire","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3548684","issn":["1049331X","15577392"],"issn_org":["1049331X"],"journal":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162003734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-390a76e2-8df8-4f47-a492-3f53d89714bd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patching Locking Bugs Statically with Crayons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382107","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"For the deployment of autonomous robotic systems in mission- and safety-critical underwater environments, aspects such as reasoning and planning need to be designed to operate in highly dynamic, uncertain environments while assuring a safe and reliable operation. However, systems are often designed or developed with safety analysis as a separate engineering process. In this paper, to tackle these challenges, we propose an initial research vision and plan with the envisioned contributions towards designing an approach for system-wide modeling and Model-Based Testing to support safety assessments of autonomous underwater robots.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Quijano, Sergio","Varshosaz, Mahsa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382404"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autonomous","Cognition","Planning","Reliability engineering","Safety","Software testing","Underwater vehicles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model based testing for system level safety of autonomous underwater robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87025378/SergioQuijano_MBT_DS_ICST2022_OpenAccess.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382404","identifier":[{"id":"85133252658","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4bea4839-72ef-47ea-8e7f-20208c6a8cfd"],"keyword":["Autonomous","Cognition","Planning","Reliability engineering","Safety","Software testing","underwater vehicles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A959F8BC35027F05EB1AFBF37DA68DE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87025378/SergioQuijano_MBT_DS_ICST2022_OpenAccess.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://remaro.eu/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/SergioQuijano_MBT_DS_ICST2022_OpenAccess.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergio","key":"quijanopau","last":"Quijano","locid":"fc57a764-276e-463a-aa68-fa54ffaf31d6","name":"Quijano, Sergio","orcid":"0000-0002-2138-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icst53961.2022.00063","eisbn":["9781665466790"],"isbn":["9781665466806"],"pages":"486-488","place":"Valencia, Spain","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2022 IEEE Conference on Software Testing, Verification and Validation (ICST)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133252658"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4bea4839-72ef-47ea-8e7f-20208c6a8cfd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Model-Based Testing for System-Level Safety of Autonomous Underwater Robots","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382404","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We perform a systematic literature review on testing, validation, and verification of robotic and autonomous systems (RAS). The scope of this review covers peer-reviewed research papers proposing, improving or evaluating testing techniques, process, or tools that address the system-level qualities of RAS. Our survey is performed based on a rigorous methodology structured in three phases. First, we made use of a set of 26 seed papers (selected by domain experts) and the SERP-TEST taxonomy to design our search query and (domain-specific) taxonomy. Second, we conducted a search in three academic search engines and applied our inclusion and exclusion criteria to the results. Respectively, we made use of related work and domain specialists (50 academics and 15 industry experts) to validate and refine the search query. As a result, we encountered 10,735 studies, out of which, 195 were included, reviewed and coded. Our objective is to answer four research questions, pertaining to (1) the type of models, (2) measures for system performance and testing adequacy, (3) tools and their availability, and (4) evidence of applicability, particularly in industrial contexts. We analyse the results of our coding to identify strengths and gaps in the domain and present recommendations to researchers and practitioners. Our findings show that variants of temporal logics are most widely used for modelling requirements and properties, while variants of state-machines and transition systems are used widely for modelling system behaviour. Other common models concern epistemic logics for specifying requirements and belief-desire-intention models for specifying system behaviour. Apart from time and epistemics, other aspects captured in models concern probabilities (e.g., for modelling uncertainty) and continuous trajectories (e.g., for modelling vehicle dynamics and kinematics). Many papers lack any rigorous measure of efficiency, effectiveness, or adequacy for their proposed techniques, processes, or tools. Among those that provide a measure of efficiency, effectiveness, or adequacy the majority use domain-agnostic generic measures such as number of failures, size of state-space or verification time were most used. There is a trend in addressing the research gap in this respect by developing domain-specific notions of performance and adequacy. Defining widely-accepted rigorous measures of performance and adequacy for each domain is an identified research gap. In terms of tools, the most widely used tools are well-established model-checkers such as Prism and Uppaal, as well as simulation tools such as Gazebo; Matlab/Simulink is another widely used toolset in this domain. Overall there is very limited evidence of industrial applicability in the papers published in this domain. There is even a gap considering consolidated benchmarks for various types of autonomous systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Araujo, Hugo","Mousavi, Mohammad Reza","Varshosaz, Mahsa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384995"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King’s College London"],"keyword":["Autonomous systems","Literature survey","Robotics","Testing","Verification and validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testing validation and verification of robotic and autonomous systems a systematic review","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3542945","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384995","identifier":[{"id":"85153787218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fdefbb26-7425-4345-b9bb-1d54e335268f"],"keyword":["Verification and validation","autonomous systems","literature survey","robotics","testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F48F3464ACEF0021BF2E51DE1DA99120"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3542945","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3542945","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King’s College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo","key":"araujopau","last":"Araujo","name":"Araujo, Hugo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Reza","key":"mousavipau","last":"Mousavi","name":"Mousavi, Mohammad Reza","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3542945","issn":["1049331X","15577392"],"journal":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology","title_org":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology (TOSEM)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153787218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fdefbb26-7425-4345-b9bb-1d54e335268f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Testing, Validation, and Verification of Robotic and Autonomous Systems: A Systematic Review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384995","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
